A||||4||Leadfoot||IAC Pintle||||1||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||07-12-2001||11:34 AM||||Even after I installed a rebuilt engine and replaced the vacuum lines my engine still has an uneven idle.  The timing is set correctly by the way.  I heard that the IAC pintle has a tendency to carbon up so I took mine off and cleaned it.  The problem is the pintle doesn't move in or out.  Could this be my problem?  I have another IAC solenoid but when I installed it the engine was idling at 2500 rpm.  Should I just bite the bullet and buy a new one?||||reg||1
Z||000001||ironhedno3||07-12-2001||11:48 AM||||go ahead and get a new one..shouldnt have any trouble finding it beings it is the same one for 85-92 camaro/firebird v6 ||||reg||6
Z||000002||terryk||07-12-2001||03:33 PM||||IAC's are servo motors and while the book implies you can push them in or out, you can't always. Also, if it's already in the fully retracted position, it won't move.<P>Start the car and disconnect the IAC. If the idle stablizes, then the IAC is changing the idle. Something is telling it to. A noisy EST signal will cause it, but that's unusual. The MAP will have little effect.<P>If the idle doesn't stablize, the IAC is not controlling it. <P>Are you getting an IAC malfunction code?<P>Don't change the IAC unless you flat out know it's bad. Did you mess with the TB?<P>A leaking EGR will cause that problem too. This is where a scanner is extremely useful.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Leadfoot||07-12-2001||03:42 PM||||I am not getting any codes and I did not touch the TB.  The EGR valve is new but the solenoid that controls it is the original.  The guy I bought the car from installed a new MAP and TPS sensor.  I'll try your suggestion and see if unplugging the IAC will stablize the idle.  I have a spare TB, MAP, TPS and IAC but God knows if they are working.  Something tells me that the spare IAC is not working since the car was idling high when I installed it. <P>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 07-12-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 07-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||07-12-2001||03:48 PM||||Don't buy a new IAC until you are sure. I have done that & haven't corrected the problem. When I installed my new engine the idle was very erratic for the 1st couple days. After that I guess the computer corrected itself somewhat. I still has some problems that have not been able to diagnose.<P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
